Introduction
The Kala Security Program is an independent cybersecurity research initiative focused on ethical hacking, digital forensics, network analysis, and security tool development. Currently, all tools and research under this program are designed and coded solely by Dr. Sai Kamesh Yadavalli, the Founder and CEO.
Open Source Statement
Selected software, tools, and research from the Kala Security Program are released as Open Source to support cybersecurity education, ethical hacking research, and security innovation.
Developers are permitted to use, study, and modify these tools while providing proper attribution.
Usage Conditions
Kala Security Program tools must only be used for ethical and legal cybersecurity activities. Use for cybercrime, unauthorized hacking, or malicious attacks is strictly prohibited.
Attribution
Any public use or distribution must include the credit: "Developed by Kala Security Program – Dr. Sai Kamesh Yadavalli".
